question:
Build an anonymous PL/SQL report that, for a given year, prints the top counties by total births. Treat the BIRTHS column as numeric (it is stored as text), skip rows where BIRTHS is not numeric, and keep the output readable (limit the number of printed rows).

Requirements:
Procedure Name: Anonymous Block.
Parameters:
None.
Output:
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Top counties by births for year=' || TO_CHAR(lv_year, 'YYYY'));
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(RPAD('County', 35) || ' | ' || LPAD('Births', 12));
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(RPAD('-', 35, '-') || '-+-' || RPAD('-', 12, '-'));
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(RPAD(rec.county_of_residence, 35) || ' | ' || LPAD(TO_CHAR(rec.total_births), 12));
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No numeric births found for year=' || TO_CHAR(lv_year, 'YYYY'));
Exception Handling:
WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN: 'No data found.'.
WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN: 'Multiple rows returned.'.
WHEN OTHERS THEN: 'Unexpected error.'.

reference_answer:
DECLARE
  co_report_limit CONSTANT PLS_INTEGER := 10; -- Limit output for report readability
  lv_year         SDOH_CDC_WONDER_NATALITY.COUNTY_NATALITY.year%TYPE;
  lv_rows_printed PLS_INTEGER := 0;
BEGIN
  -- Use a real year from the dataset to keep the script deterministic.
  SELECT MIN(cn.year)
    INTO lv_year
    FROM SDOH_CDC_WONDER_NATALITY.COUNTY_NATALITY cn;

  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Top counties by births for year=' || TO_CHAR(lv_year, 'YYYY'));
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(RPAD('County', 35) || ' | ' || LPAD('Births', 12));
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(RPAD('-', 35, '-') || '-+-' || RPAD('-', 12, '-'));

  FOR rec IN (
    SELECT cn.county_of_residence,
           SUM(TO_NUMBER(TRIM(cn.births))) AS total_births
      FROM SDOH_CDC_WONDER_NATALITY.COUNTY_NATALITY cn
     WHERE cn.year = lv_year
       AND REGEXP_LIKE(TRIM(cn.births), '^\d+$')
     GROUP BY cn.county_of_residence
     ORDER BY total_births DESC, cn.county_of_residence ASC
  ) LOOP
    EXIT WHEN lv_rows_printed >= co_report_limit;

    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(
      RPAD(rec.county_of_residence, 35) || ' | ' || LPAD(TO_CHAR(rec.total_births), 12)
    );

    lv_rows_printed := lv_rows_printed + 1;
  END LOOP;

  IF lv_rows_printed = 0 THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No numeric births found for year=' || TO_CHAR(lv_year, 'YYYY'));
  END IF;

EXCEPTION
  WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No data found.');
  WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple rows returned.');
  WHEN OTHERS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
END;

