question:
Finally, create an anonymous execution block that ties everything together for one chosen year/team: print the HR bucket report (Turn 2) and then, for the first 15 players printed, also check whether each player was an All-Star in that year and their batting league. Keep the output concise and make sure any missing league/year inputs are handled gracefully.

Requirements:
Procedure Name: Anonymous Block
Parameters:
None
Output:
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Scouting run for year=' || lv_year || ', team=' || lv_team_id || ' (max rows=' || co_report_limit || ')');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Calling bucket report...');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('All-Star check: player_id=' || r.player_id || ', year=' || lv_year || ', league=' || r.league_id || ' => ' || lv_flag);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No batting data found for the requested year/team; skipping All-Star checks.');
Exception Handling:
WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN: 'No data found.'
WHEN OTHERS THEN: 'Unexpected error.'

reference_answer:
DECLARE
  co_report_limit CONSTANT PLS_INTEGER := 15; -- Limit output for report readability

  lv_year    BASEBALL.BATTING.year%TYPE;
  lv_team_id BASEBALL.BATTING.team_id%TYPE;

  lv_found_rows PLS_INTEGER := 0;
  lv_flag       VARCHAR2(1);
BEGIN
  -- Pick a deterministic, data-backed year/team for the run.
  SELECT b.year, b.team_id
    INTO lv_year, lv_team_id
    FROM (
      SELECT b.year, b.team_id, COUNT(*) cnt
        FROM BASEBALL.BATTING b
       WHERE b.year IS NOT NULL
         AND b.team_id IS NOT NULL
       GROUP BY b.year, b.team_id
       ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC, b.year, b.team_id
    ) b
   WHERE ROWNUM = 1;

  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Scouting run for year=' || lv_year || ', team=' || lv_team_id || ' (max rows=' || co_report_limit || ')');
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Calling bucket report...');

  pkg_scouting.player_hr_buckets(
    p_year      => lv_year,
    p_team_id   => lv_team_id,
    p_high_hr   => 30,
    p_medium_hr => 10
  );

  -- After the bucket report, do concise All-Star checks for the same player set.
  FOR r IN (
    SELECT *
    FROM (
      SELECT b.player_id AS player_id,
             b.league_id AS league_id,
             SUM(b.hr) AS hr_total
        FROM BASEBALL.BATTING b
        INNER JOIN BASEBALL.PLAYER p
          ON p.player_id = b.player_id
       WHERE b.year = lv_year
         AND b.team_id = lv_team_id
         AND b.league_id IS NOT NULL
       GROUP BY b.player_id, b.league_id
       ORDER BY SUM(b.hr) DESC, b.player_id
    )
    WHERE ROWNUM <= co_report_limit
  ) LOOP
    lv_found_rows := lv_found_rows + 1;
    lv_flag := pkg_scouting.is_all_star(r.player_id, lv_year, r.league_id);
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('All-Star check: player_id=' || r.player_id || ', year=' || lv_year || ', league=' || r.league_id || ' => ' || lv_flag);
  END LOOP;

  IF lv_found_rows = 0 THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No batting data found for the requested year/team; skipping All-Star checks.');
  END IF;

EXCEPTION
  WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No data found.');
  WHEN OTHERS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
END;
/

