question:
We’re starting a quick “model health snapshot” for the stacking runs. Build an anonymous PL/SQL report that, for a given solution name and version, prints the solution summary and then lists up to 15 model scores for that solution (by step and model). If the solution doesn’t exist, print a clear message.

Requirements:
Procedure Name: Anonymous Block.
Parameters:
p_solution_name IN STACKING.SOLUTION.name%TYPE
p_version IN STACKING.SOLUTION.version%TYPE
Output:
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Solution: ' || p_solution_name || ' v' || p_version);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Correlation=' || lv_corr || ', NB_MODEL=' || lv_nb_model || ', NB_FEATURE=' || lv_nb_feature || ', SCORE=' || lv_score);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Model scores (max rows=' || co_report_limit || '):');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Step=' || rec.step || ', Model=' || rec.model || ', Train=' || rec.train_score || ', Test=' || rec.test_score);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No model scores found for this solution/version.');
Exception Handling:
WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN: 'No solution found for this name/version.'
WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN: 'Multiple solutions returned for this name/version.'
WHEN OTHERS THEN: 'Unexpected error.'

reference_answer:
DECLARE
  p_solution_name STACKING.SOLUTION.name%TYPE := 'SOLUTION_NAME_HERE';
  p_version       STACKING.SOLUTION.version%TYPE := 1;

  co_report_limit CONSTANT PLS_INTEGER := 15; -- Limit output for report readability

  lv_corr      STACKING.SOLUTION.correlation%TYPE;
  lv_nb_model  STACKING.SOLUTION.nb_model%TYPE;
  lv_nb_feature STACKING.SOLUTION.nb_feature%TYPE;
  lv_score     STACKING.SOLUTION.score%TYPE;

  lv_rows PLS_INTEGER := 0;
BEGIN
  -- Solution header
  SELECT s.correlation, s.nb_model, s.nb_feature, s.score
    INTO lv_corr, lv_nb_model, lv_nb_feature, lv_score
    FROM STACKING.SOLUTION s
   WHERE s.name = p_solution_name
     AND s.version = p_version;

  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Solution: ' || p_solution_name || ' v' || p_version);
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Correlation=' || lv_corr || ', NB_MODEL=' || lv_nb_model || ', NB_FEATURE=' || lv_nb_feature || ', SCORE=' || lv_score);

  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Model scores (max rows=' || co_report_limit || '):');

  FOR rec IN (
    SELECT ms.step, ms.model, ms.train_score, ms.test_score
      FROM STACKING.MODEL_SCORE ms
     WHERE ms.name = p_solution_name
       AND ms.version = p_version
     ORDER BY ms.step, ms.model
  ) LOOP
    EXIT WHEN lv_rows >= co_report_limit;
    lv_rows := lv_rows + 1;
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Step=' || rec.step || ', Model=' || rec.model || ', Train=' || rec.train_score || ', Test=' || rec.test_score);
  END LOOP;

  IF lv_rows = 0 THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No model scores found for this solution/version.');
  END IF;

EXCEPTION
  WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No solution found for this name/version.');
  WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple solutions returned for this name/version.');
  WHEN OTHERS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
END;
/

