question:
Operations wants a quick patient-centric snapshot. For a given patient id, list up to 15 of their most recent encounters (newest first) with the encounter class, description, and the organization name. Print each row to server output so it can be copy-pasted into a ticket. If the patient has no encounters, print a clear message and do not error.

Requirements:
Procedure Name: Anonymous Block.
Parameters: None.
Output: DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Patient = ' || lv_patient_id);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Recent encounters (max rows = ' || co_report_limit || '):');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(TO_CHAR(r.start_timestamp, 'YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI:SS') || ' | ' || r.encounterclass || ' | ' || r.description || ' | ' || r.org_name);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No encounters found for this patient.');
Exception Handling: WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN: 'No data found.'
WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN: 'Multiple rows returned.'
WHEN OTHERS THEN: 'Unexpected error.'

