question:
Your operations team wants a quick, rerunnable report showing the most recent station snapshots for a single station ID. Build a reusable routine that prints the station name and then prints up to 15 of the most recently reported status rows (bikes available, docks available, and renting/returning flags). If the station ID is NULL, handle it gracefully and print a clear message. If the station ID does not exist in station info, also handle that without crashing.

Requirements:
Procedure Name: station_ops_pkg.print_station_snapshot
Parameters:
p_station_id IN SAN_FRANCISCO_BIKESHARE.BIKESHARE_STATION_INFO.station_id%TYPE
Output:
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Station: ' || lv_station_id || ' - ' || lv_station_name);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Snapshot (most recent first), max rows = ' || co_report_limit);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('As of ' || rec.last_reported || ': bikes=' || rec.num_bikes_available || ', docks=' || rec.num_docks_available || ', renting=' || rec.is_renting || ', returning=' || rec.is_returning);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Station id is NULL.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No status rows found for this station.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No station info found for this station id.');
Exception Handling:
WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN: 'No station info found for this station id.'
WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN: 'Multiple rows returned.'
WHEN OTHERS THEN: 'Unexpected error.'

