question:
Now use the same scoring foundation to build a reusable team-level routine. Given a team id, report that team's matches, opponent, and total runs, while validating required input and handling expected exception paths cleanly.

Requirements:
Procedure Name: REPORT_TEAM_MATCH_SCORES
Parameters: p_team_id IN IPL.TEAM.TEAM_ID%TYPE
p_mode IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'NORMAL'
Output: DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Team id is required.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Team scoring report for ' || lv_team_name);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Match ' || rec.match_id || ' vs ' || rec.opponent_name || ': ' || rec.total_runs || ' runs');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No matches found for ' || lv_team_name);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No team found.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple rows returned.');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
Exception Handling: WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN: 'No team found.'
WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN: 'Multiple rows returned.'
WHEN OTHERS THEN: 'Unexpected error.'

reference_answer:
CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE report_team_match_scores(
  p_team_id IN IPL.TEAM.TEAM_ID%TYPE,
  p_mode    IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'NORMAL'
) IS
  co_report_limit CONSTANT PLS_INTEGER := 15; -- Limit output for report readability
  lv_team_name    IPL.TEAM.NAME%TYPE;
  lv_dummy_id     IPL.TEAM.TEAM_ID%TYPE;
  lv_short_text   VARCHAR2(1);
  lv_rows         NUMBER := 0;
BEGIN
  IF p_team_id IS NULL THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Team id is required.');
    RETURN;
  END IF;

  IF UPPER(p_mode) = 'MANY' THEN
    SELECT t.team_id
      INTO lv_dummy_id
      FROM IPL.TEAM t
     WHERE ROWNUM <= 2;
  ELSIF UPPER(p_mode) = 'BAD' THEN
    lv_short_text := 'TOO_LONG';
  END IF;

  SELECT t.name
    INTO lv_team_name
    FROM IPL.TEAM t
   WHERE t.team_id = p_team_id;

  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Team scoring report for ' || lv_team_name);

  FOR rec IN (
    SELECT ordered_scores.match_id,
           ordered_scores.opponent_name,
           ordered_scores.total_runs
      FROM (
            SELECT m.match_id,
                   CASE
                     WHEN m.team_1 = p_team_id THEN t2.name
                     ELSE t1.name
                   END AS opponent_name,
                   SUM(NVL(bs.runs_scored, 0) + NVL(er.extra_runs, 0)) AS total_runs
              FROM IPL.MATCH m
              INNER JOIN IPL.TEAM t1
                ON t1.team_id = m.team_1
              INNER JOIN IPL.TEAM t2
                ON t2.team_id = m.team_2
              LEFT OUTER JOIN IPL.BALL_BY_BALL b
                ON b.match_id = m.match_id
              LEFT OUTER JOIN IPL.BATSMAN_SCORED bs
                ON bs.match_id = b.match_id
               AND bs.over_id = b.over_id
               AND bs.ball_id = b.ball_id
               AND bs.innings_no = b.innings_no
              LEFT OUTER JOIN IPL.EXTRA_RUNS er
                ON er.match_id = b.match_id
               AND er.over_id = b.over_id
               AND er.ball_id = b.ball_id
               AND er.innings_no = b.innings_no
             WHERE p_team_id IN (m.team_1, m.team_2)
             GROUP BY m.match_id,
                      CASE
                        WHEN m.team_1 = p_team_id THEN t2.name
                        ELSE t1.name
                      END
             ORDER BY total_runs DESC, m.match_id
           ) ordered_scores
     WHERE ROWNUM <= co_report_limit
  ) LOOP
    lv_rows := lv_rows + 1;
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Match ' || rec.match_id || ' vs ' || rec.opponent_name || ': ' || rec.total_runs || ' runs');
  END LOOP;

  IF lv_rows = 0 THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No matches found for ' || lv_team_name);
  END IF;
EXCEPTION
  WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No team found.');
  WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple rows returned.');
  WHEN OTHERS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
END report_team_match_scores;
/

question:
Using the match totals from the earlier steps, add a small reusable function that classifies one match into a run band. The function should confirm the match exists, calculate total runs, print the band, and return a simple status value for downstream checks.

Requirements:
