question:
A junior developer tried to extend the overbooking check so it prints the airport names for both departure and arrival, but the script fails at runtime due to a mistaken SELECT...INTO that can return multiple rows. Fix the logic so it is deterministic and safe: pick exactly one row for the flight, and print the departure and arrival airport names alongside the flight number and schedule. Keep the output to 15 rows max, and make sure the exception handling still prints friendly messages.

Requirements:
Procedure Name: Anonymous Block
Parameters: None
Output: DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Flight summary for flight_id=' || lv_flight_id || ' (max rows = ' || co_report_limit || ')');
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Flight ' || lv_flight_no || ' | ' || lv_departure_airport || ' - ' || lv_departure_name || ' -> ' || lv_arrival_airport || ' - ' || lv_arrival_name);
DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Scheduled dep=' || TO_CHAR(lv_sched_dep, 'YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI') || ' | arr=' || TO_CHAR(lv_sched_arr, 'YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI'));
Exception Handling: WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN: 'No data found.'
WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN: 'Multiple rows returned.'
WHEN OTHERS THEN: 'Unexpected error.'

reference_answer:
DECLARE
  co_report_limit CONSTANT PLS_INTEGER := 15; -- Keep output small for diagnostics

  lv_flight_id         AIRLINES.FLIGHTS.flight_id%TYPE := 1;
  lv_flight_no         AIRLINES.FLIGHTS.flight_no%TYPE;
  lv_departure_airport AIRLINES.FLIGHTS.departure_airport%TYPE;
  lv_arrival_airport   AIRLINES.FLIGHTS.arrival_airport%TYPE;
  lv_sched_dep         AIRLINES.FLIGHTS.scheduled_departure%TYPE;
  lv_sched_arr         AIRLINES.FLIGHTS.scheduled_arrival%TYPE;

  lv_departure_name    AIRLINES.AIRPORTS_DATA.airport_name%TYPE;
  lv_arrival_name      AIRLINES.AIRPORTS_DATA.airport_name%TYPE;
BEGIN
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Flight summary for flight_id=' || lv_flight_id || ' (max rows = ' || co_report_limit || ')');

  -- Debugging fix: ensure the SELECT...INTO is single-row by filtering on primary identifier.
  SELECT f.flight_no,
         f.departure_airport,
         f.arrival_airport,
         f.scheduled_departure,
         f.scheduled_arrival
    INTO lv_flight_no,
         lv_departure_airport,
         lv_arrival_airport,
         lv_sched_dep,
         lv_sched_arr
    FROM AIRLINES.FLIGHTS f
   WHERE f.flight_id = lv_flight_id;

  SELECT a.airport_name
    INTO lv_departure_name
    FROM AIRLINES.AIRPORTS_DATA a
   WHERE a.airport_code = lv_departure_airport;

  SELECT a.airport_name
    INTO lv_arrival_name
    FROM AIRLINES.AIRPORTS_DATA a
   WHERE a.airport_code = lv_arrival_airport;

  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Flight ' || lv_flight_no || ' | ' || lv_departure_airport || ' - ' || lv_departure_name || ' -> ' || lv_arrival_airport || ' - ' || lv_arrival_name);
  DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Scheduled dep=' || TO_CHAR(lv_sched_dep, 'YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI') || ' | arr=' || TO_CHAR(lv_sched_arr, 'YYYY-MM-DD HH24:MI'));

EXCEPTION
  WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('No data found.');
  WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Multiple rows returned.');
  WHEN OTHERS THEN
    DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE('Unexpected error.');
END;
/

